# modbusspec-sweep 0: requests to a real device in the order sent, and their replies
device: inverter/huawei/sun2000
product: 'Huawei SUN2000-15K-MB0 (firmware V200R022D02, software V200R023C10SPC211) with a LUNA2000 battery of 3 packs
  (LUNA2000-7-E1, 20.7 kWh), read through the EMMA'
unit: 2
link: 'Modbus TCP, port 502, to the EMMA, which answers for units 0, 2 and 4; its Modbus TCP set to restricted, the client on the allow-list'
date: 2026-11-02, from 10:31:12 (+01:00), about 3 s for all three units
tool: 'read_documented.py, read only (function 03): one request per register that huawei-solar-lib lists for this device (commit 039d542,
  src/huawei_solar/registers.py, parsed without running it), at its address and length, no blocks; sent again only after a connection error'
site: 'the house also has an SMA inverter (AC-coupled); no external meter at the EMMA; the battery was charging at about 3.5 kW'
masked: 'digits of serial numbers (30015, 31015, 37052, 38200, 38242, 38284) as #; their letters are kept. Every character of the battery
  register code (37954) as ?'
format: 'function address+count[*runs] reply. A run of n requests: each starting where the one before ended, same count, same reply. Reply: E code for an
  exception, S for no reply, or the words in hex, w*n for n equal words, M and two characters for a masked word (# a hidden digit, ? a hidden character).'
